<title>GERMANY: Cologne Re 95 net rises 72 pct.</title>
<headline>Cologne Re 95 net rises 72 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurer Koelnische Rueckversicherung  AG (Cologne Re) said its 1995 group net profit rose 72 percent to 125.2 million marks from 72.7 million marks a year earlier.</p>
<p>The company said DVFA per-share profits rose to 113.80 marks from 112.85 marks.</p>
<p>Premium income fell 3.8 percent to 5.5 billion marks, which the company traced to currency fluctuations and other factors.</p>
<p>Cologne Re is controlled by U.S. reinsurer General Re Corp.</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom, 49 228 260 97160</p>
